# Ajilamu TLS front door.
#
# The first address is the custom name. Its A record is DNS-only, so the
# ACME HTTP-01 challenge reaches this origin directly. The second address
# arrives from the systemd drop-in that bootstrap.sh writes. It encodes the
# reserved address with dashes under sslip.io and stays the fallback when the
# custom certificate cannot be issued.
#
# Caddy obtains one public certificate per name over the HTTP-01 challenge.
#
# flush_interval -1 disables response buffering, so the run event stream
# arrives frame by frame instead of at the end of the run. Range requests and
# their 206 answers pass through the proxy untouched, so video scrubbing
# never re-downloads the file.
ajilamu.nryn.dev, {$AJILAMU_HOSTNAME} {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}
